# Portability patches (format and list: docs/UPSTREAM_CHANGES.md).
patch: jambu-simon96-nonce-in-bounds
why: jambu_initialization reads 8 bytes from the 6-byte nonce and masks off the 2 extra bytes: the value is right on
why: little-endian targets, but the read runs 2 bytes past the nonce (AddressSanitizer heap-buffer-overflow, CI run
why: 45581879065). The patch copies the 6 nonce bytes into a zeroed word, the same value without the over-read.
file: upstream/ref/encrypt_simon96.c
count: 1
find: 	stateS[0] = (((uint64_t *)iv)[0] & 0xffffffffffff); stateS[1] = 0; 
replace: 	stateS[0] = 0; memcpy(&stateS[0], iv, 6); stateS[1] = 0; 
patch: unaligned-simon-c-line-25
why: The reference code reads and writes block words through casts of byte pointers (for example ((unsigned int *)(c+msglen))[0]),
why: which are misaligned typed accesses (undefined behaviour, UBSan "misaligned address" in CI run 45610244076). The patch moves the
why: bytes with memcpy to or from a local of the same type (helper functions added in the same file). The value is the native-order
why: word the cast read or wrote, so every output is bit-identical on every target.
file: upstream/ref/Simon.c
count: 1
find: rkexp[i] = ((uint32_t *)rk)[i];
replace: rkexp[i] = jb_ld32(rk, i);
patch: unaligned-simon-c-line-42
why: The reference code reads and writes block words through casts of byte pointers (for example ((unsigned int *)(c+msglen))[0]),
why: which are misaligned typed accesses (undefined behaviour, UBSan "misaligned address" in CI run 45610244076). The patch moves the
why: bytes with memcpy to or from a local of the same type (helper functions added in the same file). The value is the native-order
why: word the cast read or wrote, so every output is bit-identical on every target.
file: upstream/ref/Simon.c
count: 1
find: rkexp[0] = (((uint64_t *)rk)[0]) & 0xffffffffffff;
replace: rkexp[0] = (jb_ld64(rk, 0)) & 0xffffffffffff;
